{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "policy": "ADR-0013 layering, narrowed by ADR-0016 (WI-OI-102c). Every workspace unit has exactly one layer. core: the kernel only (identity and sessions, tenancy, roles and policy, versioned configuration and settings, module registry, persistence, events and jobs, audit and retention, observability, API and UI conventions). capability:<name>: packages of a capability product (the groups under capabilityPackages) that any solution may select; a capability may also be a module (spec.category: capability). module:<key>: code owned by one business or capability module (modules/<key>/** is always module-owned). shell: composition roots (the web app and the module host), which may import anything. tooling: tests and build tooling, not shipped. Kernel code must not import capability or module code; a capability must not import another capability's or a module's code. retiring lists packages that WI-OI-102f removes (ADR-0016 F3). A new workspace package must be added here before it builds (audit:layers fails on unclassified units).",
  "shell": [
    "apps/workflow-platform",
    "apps/module-host"
  ],
  "tooling": [
    "e2e"
  ],
  "coreApps": [
    "apps/playground-api"
  ],
